Diagram: triangle $APB$ with $PA = 7$ km, $PB = 9$ km, $\angle APB = 65^\circ$, $AB = 8.76\ldots$ km.

\exfigure{33_q15_1}

$$\begin{aligned} AB^2 &= 7^2 + 9^2 - 2\times 7\times 9\cos 65^\circ \\ &= 76.75\ldots \\ AB &= 8.76 \text{ km} \end{aligned}$$

$$\begin{aligned} AB &= 80 \div 10 \\ &= 8 \text{ cm} \\ \angle AOB &= 360^\circ \div 10 = 36^\circ \\ \angle OAB &= \dfrac{180^\circ - 36^\circ}{2} \\ &= 72^\circ \end{aligned}$$

\exfigure{33_q22_1}

$$\begin{aligned} \dfrac{r}{\sin 72^\circ} &= \dfrac{8}{\sin 36^\circ} \\ r &= 12.944\ldots \\ \text{Area} &= 10 \times \dfrac{1}{2}\times (12.944\ldots)^2 \times \sin 36^\circ \\ &\doteqdot 492.4 \text{ cm}^2 \end{aligned}$$

